    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside trio of **Corbin Carroll** (84.80), **Mickey Moniak** (75.74), and **Josh Naylor** (74.13). **Corbin Carroll** is our strongest play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Junk, who carries a 4.71 xERA; the combination of a high-ceiling park and favorable platoon positioning makes him a primary target for stolen base production, our most critical category. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** draws a massive +14% score boost from park factors and dynamic platoon alignment against Buehler. **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) also projects as an elite start, as his high-leverage spot in the two-hole against the left-handed P\u00e9rez creates an optimal environment for run production despite the pitcher\u2019s respectable xERA.\n\nOn the margins, we are keeping a close eye on **Gabriel Moreno** (69.86) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (65.35), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against Junk and Brown, respectively. The most difficult decision in today's setup was leaving **Austin Riley** (55.98) on the bench. While his talent is clear, the optimizer faded him against Gausman\u2019s 3.75 xERA, prioritizing the aggressive stolen base profiles of players like **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero**. While **Jose Caballero** (55.02) carries a lower raw score due to his nine-hole positioning, his ability to capitalize on a favorable delivery window makes him a necessary pivot over **Austin Riley** to chase the scarce SB category.\n\nWe remain cautious of the volatility surrounding **Moises Ballesteros** (46.06) and **Zach McKinstry** (46.06), both of whom sit right at our efficiency floor; any late-breaking weather shifts or lineup adjustments could force us to re-evaluate their roles to preserve our game caps. **James Wood** remains on the bench despite an elite xwOBA of .413, as his current inactive status in the official lineup mandates an automated score of 0.00. We will continue to monitor the status of **Travis Bazzana** and **Trevor Story** to ensure we are maximizing every plate appearance as we chase the 5x5 Roto title.",
